started calling me Imoko.

259
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:06,620
Um, well, I, I can do that.

260
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:10,680
And I want you to call me Yomuko.

261
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:12,060
You got it.

262
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,860
I will, Yomuko!

263
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,400
That's weird.

264
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:19,820
I've never felt this way before.

265
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:21,880
Could this be?

266
00:18:23,540 --> 00:18:28,200
I used to think creators needed
loneliness to fuel their creativity.

267
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:30,300
But I think I was wrong.

268
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:33,340
One creative person alone creates a spark.

269
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,760
But when we come together,
that's a bonfire.

270
00:18:37,080 --> 00:18:41,137
When I think of it that way, some of the
boring stories on here start to make sense.

271
00:18:41,220 --> 00:18:44,808
It might just be because the
writers didn't have any friends.

272
00:18:58,900 --> 00:18:59,837
Chainsmoker Cat!

273
00:18:59,920 --> 00:19:00,861
Chainsmoker Cat!

274
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,000
Today's a rare treat.

275
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:13,617
Imoko is staying over at her
friend's house, so I'm all alone.

276
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:16,140
Time for a nice, quiet evening alone.

277
00:19:23,020 --> 00:19:25,200
Tarjeeling tea always hits the spot.

278
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:27,000
What a delightful aroma.

279
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:32,497
And these cookies I hid from
Imoko are so delicious, too.

280
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:39,220
But most importantly, tea and sweets are
best enjoyed with a cigarette on the side.

281
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,200
I'll never get tired of this.

282
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:51,520
Oh no, I must have fallen asleep.

283
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,060
I wonder what time it is now.

284
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:56,536
Oh no, the room is filled with smoke!

285
00:19:57,020 --> 00:20:00,637
I haven't seen this much since
my honeymoon vacation in London.

286
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,340
I guess I got carried away.

287
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:06,254
I'm sure all this smoke will
be out of here by tomorrow.

288
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,500
Oh, perfect. It's Imoko.

289
00:20:10,320 --> 00:20:13,160
Hi, Mom. It's me. Yes, honey. I hear you.

290
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:15,620
I'm guessing you're having fun. Yay!

291
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:17,697
I'm coming home sooner than I thought.

292
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:18,610
What?

293
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:19,530
It's awful.

294
00:20:19,613 --> 00:20:22,317
It looks like there was a
break-in at Hana's house, so...

295
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:24,417
A break-in means you have to come home?

296
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:27,317
The good news is that there
wasn't really any major damage,

297
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,988
but they called the police.

298
00:20:29,140 --> 00:20:31,777
Hana was especially pissed
since they stole her panties.

299
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:34,220
Oh, stolen panties aren't fun.

300
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,897
So anyway, I'll be home
in about ten minutes.

301
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:38,317
Oh, and don't stress about dinner.

302
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,230
I ate already.

303
00:20:39,313 --> 00:20:40,143
Be home soon!

304
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:43,130
Oh, crap.

305
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:44,888
I don't have a lot of time.

306
00:20:46,980 --> 00:20:48,274
Why is this happening?

307
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:51,397
I didn't do anything wrong,
so why am I being punished?

308
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:54,817
If only there hadn't been that
stupid break-in at Hanna's house!

309
00:20:54,900 --> 00:20:56,841
Why does break-in mean come home?

310
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:02,820
I'm back, Mom!

311
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,700
Wow, it stinks in here!

312
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,720
I know you're not smoking again, right?

313
00:21:11,340 --> 00:21:12,170
Mom?

314
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,640
What happened to you?

315
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:19,497
Let me get you out of this!

316
00:21:19,580 --> 00:21:20,410
Hold on!

317
00:21:22,260 --> 00:21:23,340
Oh, darling.

318
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:27,371
After our phone call, a scary
burglar broke into the house.

319
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:29,348
Just look at what they did.

320
00:21:30,940 --> 00:21:31,770
No way!

321
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,920
I'm just so grateful they didn't hurt me.

322
00:21:35,240 --> 00:21:38,200
But the man who did this,
he just smoked so much.

323
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:41,032
He looked like he was some kind of demon.

324
00:21:41,580 --> 00:21:42,933
You're really not hurt?

325
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:43,870
You're okay?

326
00:21:44,140 --> 00:21:45,800
Yes, my darling, I'm fine.

327
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:57,497
I promise I will never, ever stay
over at a prince's house ever again!

328
00:21:57,580 --> 00:21:58,580
Don't be silly.

329
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:00,497
Oh, honey, don't worry about me.

330
00:22:00,580 --> 00:22:02,051
Go as much as you'd like.

331
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:04,141
I'll never leave you alone again!

332
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,877
Yeah, yeah,

333
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:37,960
yeah.

334
00:22:58,300 --> 00:23:01,657
Why do we know how people are here?

335
00:23:01,740 --> 00:23:05,040
Maybe they're in trouble,
but they're in trouble,

336
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:08,057
and they're in trouble,
but they're in trouble.

337
00:23:08,140 --> 00:23:09,258
They're in trouble,

338
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:10,971
or if they're in trouble,

339
00:23:12,500 --> 00:23:16,740
and they're in trouble,
even if they're in trouble.

340
00:23:17,040 --> 00:23:20,737
I'll say this is a dream, but I
don't believe that we're still here.

341
00:23:20,820 --> 00:23:24,040
I don't want to worry.

342
00:23:57,580 --> 00:23:58,410
Thank you.

343
00:24:27,580 --> 00:24:28,410
Thank you.

344
00:24:58,560 --> 00:25:00,000
Thank you.
